++  citations: {"ok": true, "contract_version": "4", "command": "citations", "records": [{"citation_id": "cite-20261018-001", "issue": 613, "play": "/intent", "question": "What path does a shopper take from the storefront to paying?", "answer": "Home, category pages, product listing, product detail, cart, then checkout.", "decided_by": "intent-resolver (/intent)", "decided_at": "2026-10-18T19:01:23Z", "trace": [{"asked": "Which domain is this product in?", "found": "Ecommerce: the shop sells goods — catalog, cart, orders, storefront.", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/ecommerce.md", "start": 5, "end": 5, "fingerprint": "sha256:6b5ec069a363310f568b9f09f8c68e1dd5b35b45df74d5879cd69dcfbcd0301d", "text": "  trigger: \"the product sells physical or digital goods — catalog, cart, orders, storefront\"", "version": "5fcd88e05cf6", "around": {"start": 2, "end": 8, "text": "id: domains/ecommerce\ntitle: \"Ecommerce: how we build it — content-first MACH, selected on the commerce↔content spectrum\"\nconditions:\n  trigger: \"the product sells physical or digital goods — catalog, cart, orders, storefront\"\n  selection_keys: [commerce-vs-content-weight, sku-count, traffic-volume, merchandising-depth, nfr.performance]\nprovenance: interview (#434) + an eCommerce selection-criterion reference\n---"}}}, {"asked": "What journey must an ecommerce product always have?", "found": "The core journey: home, category pages, product listing, product detail, cart, checkout handoff.", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/ecommerce.md", "start": 87, "end": 88, "fingerprint": "sha256:7fe917d2d71c88a49db9745f6170abe113db7fe23863f36e7f921ad19163a6b5", "text": "**home → category pages → PLP (product listing) → PDP (product detail) → cart →\ncheckout handoff.**", "version": "5fcd88e05cf6", "around": {"start": 84, "end": 91, "text": "Start with the basics and make sure the core is always present. Without it the\njourney breaks, no matter the quadrant:\n\n**home → category pages → PLP (product listing) → PDP (product detail) → cart →\ncheckout handoff.**\n\nBuild this spine first, end to end, before any enrichment. Everything else hangs\noff it."}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261018-002", "issue": 613, "play": "/vision", "question": "How does the shop take card payments?", "answer": "Through a payment provider with hosted fields, so card data never touches our servers.", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper (/vision)", "decided_at": "2026-10-18T19:01:24Z", "trace": [{"asked": "Does the shop take money?", "found": "Yes: monetization is paywall.", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/profile.yaml", "start": 7, "end": 7, "fingerprint": "sha256:8071569efe1aadc32e2d666855ee1fe766445fb6fb3f30ba3d592a8a19df0377", "text": "    monetization: paywall", "version": null, "around": {"start": 4, "end": 10, "text": "  shape:\n    stage: public\n    users: public\n    monetization: paywall\n    surfaces: [web, mobile]\n  nfr:\n    performance:   { level: high, gate: \"p95 page load under 2 s\" }"}}}, {"asked": "Which domain covers taking money?", "found": "Payments, not ecommerce.", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/ecommerce.md", "start": 22, "end": 22, "fingerprint": "sha256:29199abd32c9e7c4524dd6347d3986b03b2822cc548b5e62a2382e7da43db14b", "text": "Taking money is a separate concern — see `payments`. What to charge and on what", "version": "5fcd88e05cf6", "around": {"start": 19, "end": 25, "text": "the domain is organised around the intents people bring to it, and capabilities are\nhow we satisfy them. Agentic features route and act on these intents directly.\n\nTaking money is a separate concern — see `payments`. What to charge and on what\nplan — see `billing`. The CMS/DAM that backs \"content leads the glass\" — see\n`content-management`. Search and recommendations — see `experience`.\n"}}}, {"asked": "What is the payments stance?", "found": "Never hold card data you don't have to: charge through a PSP with hosted fields and tokenisation.", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/payments.md", "start": 19, "end": 21, "fingerprint": "sha256:a7616b3002d1670c52f7fb9d8bcc8a80d4b9d5a354daddbcf7c433e3bad6ab39", "text": "The one organising rule: **never hold card data you don't have to.** Charge through\na **PSP** (Stripe/Adyen/etc.) with **hosted fields / tokenisation**, so you stay\nout of the worst of PCI scope. Payments is **trust infrastructure** — almost every", "version": "5fcd88e05cf6", "around": {"start": 16, "end": 24, "text": "> as the commerce-heavy quadrants in `ecommerce`.\n\n## Stance (proposed)\nThe one organising rule: **never hold card data you don't have to.** Charge through\na **PSP** (Stripe/Adyen/etc.) with **hosted fields / tokenisation**, so you stay\nout of the worst of PCI scope. Payments is **trust infrastructure** — almost every\nchoice here is pulled by `nfr.security` or a `compliance` regime (PCI-DSS is\nusually one).\n"}}}, {"asked": "What is the floor for card payments?", "found": "Card via PSP with hosted fields.", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/payments.md", "start": 44, "end": 44, "fingerprint": "sha256:fd7868764e0280c165b2ef7106df640b30e3686d1bae635bfb9f2ed6fd113892", "text": "  - Card via PSP / hosted fields — charge through Stripe/Adyen with hosted fields so card data never touches your servers. The floor.", "version": "5fcd88e05cf6", "around": {"start": 41, "end": 47, "text": "## Capabilities (selected by risk, scale, regime)\n- **Payment Processing** — the floor: card via PSP; bank transfer/ACH/wallets when\n  the region or user base expects non-card rails. Tokenise; never store raw PANs.\n  - Card via PSP / hosted fields — charge through Stripe/Adyen with hosted fields so card data never touches your servers. The floor.\n  - Tokenised vaulting — store a PSP token in place of the PAN for later charges. The floor whenever you reuse a method; mandatory when `compliance` includes PCI-DSS.\n  - Bank transfer / ACH — direct-debit / bank rails for lower-fee or non-card payers. Add when `shape.users: public` and a broad consumer base expects them.\n  - Wallets — Apple Pay / Google Pay one-tap. Add when `shape.surfaces` includes mobile."}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261018-003", "issue": 613, "play": "/vision", "question": "Can a returning shopper pay with a saved card?", "answer": "Yes, as a provider token only — never the card number.", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper (/vision)", "decided_at": "2026-10-18T19:01:24Z", "trace": [{"asked": "What security level and compliance does the profile set?", "found": "Security is high; PCI-DSS and GDPR are in force.", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/profile.yaml", "start": 11, "end": 14, "fingerprint": "sha256:792104d6b9ddcfb5eb567bd3e3e3173bce8d6c5a3d5296a223484131bb3c935a", "text": "    security:      { level: high, gate: \"OWASP ASVS L2; no P1/P2\" }\n    accessibility: { level: high, gate: \"WCAG 2.1 AA\" }\n    privacy:       { level: high, gate: \"PII encrypted at rest and in transit\" }\n  compliance: [PCI-DSS, GDPR]", "version": null, "around": {"start": 8, "end": 14, "text": "    surfaces: [web, mobile]\n  nfr:\n    performance:   { level: high, gate: \"p95 page load under 2 s\" }\n    security:      { level: high, gate: \"OWASP ASVS L2; no P1/P2\" }\n    accessibility: { level: high, gate: \"WCAG 2.1 AA\" }\n    privacy:       { level: high, gate: \"PII encrypted at rest and in transit\" }\n  compliance: [PCI-DSS, GDPR]"}}}, {"asked": "What does a saved card need under PCI-DSS?", "found": "Tokenised vaulting is the floor and mandatory under PCI-DSS: store the PSP token, never the card.", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/payments.md", "start": 63, "end": 65, "fingerprint": "sha256:85ad97c8e33a8641f2dee207bc6f564dddb4fad2d0a1394feb5feb96b3aa165e", "text": "- **Saved Methods / One-Click** — when repeat purchase or conversion speed matters;\n  tokenised vaulting only (mandatory under PCI-DSS).\n  - Tokenised vaulting — store the PSP token, never the card, for one-click reuse. The floor of this capability; mandatory when `compliance` includes PCI-DSS.", "version": "5fcd88e05cf6", "around": {"start": 60, "end": 68, "text": "  - Level 1 — full / partial refunds: reverse a charge in whole or part via the PSP. The floor.\n  - Level 2 — chargeback handling: receive and process issuer-initiated reversals. Add when `shape.monetization: monetized`.\n  - Level 3 — dispute-evidence workflow: assemble and submit evidence with an audit trail. Add when `nfr.observability >= high`, or `compliance` includes PCI-DSS.\n- **Saved Methods / One-Click** — when repeat purchase or conversion speed matters;\n  tokenised vaulting only (mandatory under PCI-DSS).\n  - Tokenised vaulting — store the PSP token, never the card, for one-click reuse. The floor of this capability; mandatory when `compliance` includes PCI-DSS.\n  - One-click checkout — charge a saved token without re-entry. Add when `shape.monetization: monetized` and repeat purchase matters.\n\n## Where it goes wrong (proposed)"}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261018-004", "issue": 613, "play": "/vision", "question": "Are Apple Pay and Google Pay part of launch?", "answer": "Yes. The shop has a mobile app, so wallets are in.", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper (/vision)", "decided_at": "2026-10-18T19:01:24Z", "trace": [{"asked": "Who are the shop's users, and where do they use it?", "found": "The public, on web and mobile.", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/profile.yaml", "start": 6, "end": 8, "fingerprint": "sha256:ea4be5fa81c618857bc9e02deec8eb38b782ca54725daf5ca6c452edfeaf77fd", "text": "    users: public\n    monetization: paywall\n    surfaces: [web, mobile]", "version": null, "around": {"start": 3, "end": 11, "text": "  state: set\n  shape:\n    stage: public\n    users: public\n    monetization: paywall\n    surfaces: [web, mobile]\n  nfr:\n    performance:   { level: high, gate: \"p95 page load under 2 s\" }\n    security:      { level: high, gate: \"OWASP ASVS L2; no P1/P2\" }"}}}, {"asked": "When are wallets included?", "found": "Add wallets when the surfaces include mobile.", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/payments.md", "start": 47, "end": 47, "fingerprint": "sha256:bc8ec15bae47abe96db5d0e267587d42041ad8fc38915131f6c38acfc63f172e", "text": "  - Wallets — Apple Pay / Google Pay one-tap. Add when `shape.surfaces` includes mobile.", "version": "5fcd88e05cf6", "around": {"start": 44, "end": 50, "text": "  - Card via PSP / hosted fields — charge through Stripe/Adyen with hosted fields so card data never touches your servers. The floor.\n  - Tokenised vaulting — store a PSP token in place of the PAN for later charges. The floor whenever you reuse a method; mandatory when `compliance` includes PCI-DSS.\n  - Bank transfer / ACH — direct-debit / bank rails for lower-fee or non-card payers. Add when `shape.users: public` and a broad consumer base expects them.\n  - Wallets — Apple Pay / Google Pay one-tap. Add when `shape.surfaces` includes mobile.\n- **Checkout / Payment UX** — accessible payment screens (`nfr.accessibility`);\n  localised currency and methods across regions. (Pairs with `ecommerce`.)\n  - Hosted / redirect checkout — PSP-hosted page or drop-in widget that keeps you out of PCI scope. The floor."}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261018-005", "issue": 613, "play": "/vision", "question": "Is guest checkout allowed at launch?", "answer": "Yes. An account is offered after payment.", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper (/vision)", "decided_at": "2026-10-18T19:01:25Z", "trace": [{"asked": "Who are the shop's users, and where do they use it?", "found": "The public, on web and mobile.", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/profile.yaml", "start": 6, "end": 8, "fingerprint": "sha256:ea