3, "end": 11, "text": "  state: set\n  shape:\n    stage: public\n    users: public\n    monetization: paywall\n    surfaces: [web, mobile]\n  nfr:\n    performance:   { level: high, gate: \"p95 page load under 2 s\" }\n    security:      { level: high, gate: \"OWASP ASVS L2; no P1/P2\" }"}}}, {"asked": "Which domain covers sign-in, and what decides its parts?", "found": "User management. Its parts are picked by the profile: the users, the surfaces, security, accessibility and compliance.", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/user-management.md", "start": 4, "end": 6, "fingerprint": "sha256:e295931e169cff7ce46dfc8847509d1797cde5adcfe9ec5770941dfd04f3273e", "text": "conditions:\n  trigger: \"the product needs accounts, login, profiles, roles, or access control\"\n  selection_keys: [shape.users, shape.surfaces, nfr.security, nfr.accessibility, compliance]", "version": "5fcd88e05cf6", "around": {"start": 1, "end": 9, "text": "---\nid: domains/user-management\ntitle: \"User Management: capabilities and when to include each (profile-driven)\"\nconditions:\n  trigger: \"the product needs accounts, login, profiles, roles, or access control\"\n  selection_keys: [shape.users, shape.surfaces, nfr.security, nfr.accessibility, compliance]\nprovenance: seeded\n---\n"}}}, {"asked": "What security level and compliance does the profile set?", "found": "Security is high; PCI-DSS and GDPR are in force.", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/profile.yaml", "start": 11, "end": 14, "fingerprint": "sha256:792104d6b9ddcfb5eb567bd3e3e3173bce8d6c5a3d5296a223484131bb3c935a", "text": "    security:      { level: high, gate: \"OWASP ASVS L2; no P1/P2\" }\n    accessibility: { level: high, gate: \"WCAG 2.1 AA\" }\n    privacy:       { level: high, gate: \"PII encrypted at rest and in transit\" }\n  compliance: [PCI-DSS, GDPR]", "version": null, "around": {"start": 8, "end": 14, "text": "    surfaces: [web, mobile]\n  nfr:\n    performance:   { level: high, gate: \"p95 page load under 2 s\" }\n    security:      { level: high, gate: \"OWASP ASVS L2; no P1/P2\" }\n    accessibility: { level: high, gate: \"WCAG 2.1 AA\" }\n    privacy:       { level: high, gate: \"PII encrypted at rest and in transit\" }\n  compliance: [PCI-DSS, GDPR]"}}}, {"asked": "Which sign-in methods do those values select?", "found": "Email and password is the floor; social login because the users are public; MFA because security is high and PCI-DSS is in force.", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/user-management.md", "start": 44, "end": 47, "fingerprint": "sha256:001365eca3509fec072c26b605372ed8719be8d71efd80c08e780fb6aee613b9", "text": "- **Authentication** — include when users sign in.\n  - Email & password — the default credential login (the floor).\n  - Social login — when `shape.users: public` and signup friction matters.\n  - MFA — when `nfr.security >= high`, or `compliance` includes SOC2 / HIPAA / PCI-DSS.", "version": "5fcd88e05cf6", "around": {"start": 41, "end": 50, "text": "Read each line as \"include X when {profile condition}\". Start at the floor; add\nonly when a profile dimension calls for it.\n\n- **Authentication** — include when users sign in.\n  - Email & password — the default credential login (the floor).\n  - Social login — when `shape.users: public` and signup friction matters.\n  - MFA — when `nfr.security >= high`, or `compliance` includes SOC2 / HIPAA / PCI-DSS.\n  - Passwordless — when `nfr.security >= high` and you want to remove password risk entirely.\n  - Enterprise SSO — when the user base is organizations (B2B), or `compliance` requires federated identity.\n- **Registration** — include when users create accounts."}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261018-009", "issue": 613, "play": "/understand", "question": "Does the shop need MFA at launch?", "answer": "Yes. Security is high and PCI-DSS is in force; either one brings MFA.", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper (/understand)", "decided_at": "2026-10-18T19:01:25Z", "trace": [{"asked": "What security level and compliance does the profile set?", "found": "Security is high; PCI-DSS and GDPR are in force.", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/profile.yaml", "start": 11, "end": 14, "fingerprint": "sha256:792104d6b9ddcfb5eb567bd3e3e3173bce8d6c5a3d5296a223484131bb3c935a", "text": "    security:      { level: high, gate: \"OWASP ASVS L2; no P1/P2\" }\n    accessibility: { level: high, gate: \"WCAG 2.1 AA\" }\n    privacy:       { level: high, gate: \"PII encrypted at rest and in transit\" }\n  compliance: [PCI-DSS, GDPR]", "version": null, "around": {"start": 8, "end": 14, "text": "    surfaces: [web, mobile]\n  nfr:\n    performance:   { level: high, gate: \"p95 page load under 2 s\" }\n    security:      { level: high, gate: \"OWASP ASVS L2; no P1/P2\" }\n    accessibility: { level: high, gate: \"WCAG 2.1 AA\" }\n    privacy:       { level: high, gate: \"PII encrypted at rest and in transit\" }\n  compliance: [PCI-DSS, GDPR]"}}}, {"asked": "When is MFA included?", "found": "When security is high or more, or compliance includes PCI-DSS.", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/user-management.md", "start": 47, "end": 47, "fingerprint": "sha256:c89448a174063a7fd38563ddc89c1a0248c42701647a0f1bd7b13b280b2c293e", "text": "  - MFA — when `nfr.security >= high`, or `compliance` includes SOC2 / HIPAA / PCI-DSS.", "version": "5fcd88e05cf6", "around": {"start": 44, "end": 50, "text": "- **Authentication** — include when users sign in.\n  - Email & password — the default credential login (the floor).\n  - Social login — when `shape.users: public` and signup friction matters.\n  - MFA — when `nfr.security >= high`, or `compliance` includes SOC2 / HIPAA / PCI-DSS.\n  - Passwordless — when `nfr.security >= high` and you want to remove password risk entirely.\n  - Enterprise SSO — when the user base is organizations (B2B), or `compliance` requires federated identity.\n- **Registration** — include when users create accounts."}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261018-010", "issue": 613, "play": "/understand", "question": "Which refunds are in launch?", "answer": "Full and partial refunds through the payment provider. Chargeback handling waits.", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper (/understand)", "decided_at": "2026-10-18T19:01:26Z", "trace": [{"asked": "What is the refunds floor?", "found": "Full and partial refunds through the PSP.", "source": {"tier": "phoenix", "path": "knowledge/domains/payments.md", "start": 60, "end": 60, "fingerprint": "sha256:9917ad82b9768f99546cca1c1836396623548c3997c552b6165b23149a133e2d", "text": "  - Level 1 — full / partial refunds: reverse a charge in whole or part via the PSP. The floor.", "version": "5fcd88e05cf6", "around": {"start": 57, "end": 63, "text": "  - Level 3 — manual review queue: flagged transactions held for human decision. Add when `nfr.security >= xhigh`, or `compliance` includes PCI-DSS.\n- **Refunds & Disputes** — full/partial refunds; chargeback handling; dispute\n  evidence workflow when a regime or volume requires the audit trail.\n  - Level 1 — full / partial refunds: reverse a charge in whole or part via the PSP. The floor.\n  - Level 2 — chargeback handling: receive and process issuer-initiated reversals. Add when `shape.monetization: monetized`.\n  - Level 3 — dispute-evidence workflow: assemble and submit evidence with an audit trail. Add when `nfr.observability >= high`, or `compliance` includes PCI-DSS.\n- **Saved Methods / One-Click** — when repeat purchase or conversion speed matters;"}}}, {"asked": "Does the shop's monetization call for more?", "found": "Monetization is paywall.", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/profile.yaml", "start": 7, "end": 7, "fingerprint": "sha256:8071569efe1aadc32e2d666855ee1fe766445fb6fb3f30ba3d592a8a19df0377", "text": "    monetization: paywall", "version": null, "around": {"start": 4, "end": 10, "text